from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" is value "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r - l + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Two pieces of the fence from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l2"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r2"},{"kind":"text","text":" are called matching, if the following conditions hold:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pieces do not intersect, that is, there isn't a single plank, such that it occurs in both pieces of the fence; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pieces are of the same width; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" for all "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0 ≤ i ≤ r1 - l1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" the following condition holds: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"hl1 + i + hl2 + i = hl1 + hl2"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"John chose a few pieces of the fence and now wants to know how many distinct matching pieces are for each of them. Two pieces of the fence are distinct if there is a plank, which belongs to one of them and does not belong to the other one."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of wood planks in the fence. The second line contains "},{"kind":"m